## 3. What the Machine Eats

### 3.1 The raw modes

**[Proven]** The machine consumes single-frequency modes of the lattice. A single-frequency mode is a plane wave `(k₁, k₂)` on the torus, where `k₁, k₂ ∈ {0, 1, ..., 7}`.

**[Proven]** The lattice has 64 raw modes (one per site in frequency space).

**[Proven]** The raw modes are the machine's input. They're the "raw material."

### 3.2 The symmetries

**[Proven]** The torus has four spin structures, corresponding to periodic (+) or anti-periodic (−) boundary conditions on each of the two cycles.

**[Proven]** The four spin structures are:
- (+,+): periodic in both directions
- (+,−): periodic in x, anti-periodic in y
- (−,+): anti-periodic in x, periodic in y
- (−,−): anti-periodic in both directions

**[Proven]** Each spin structure has its own Laplacian. Each has its own eigenmodes.

**[Proven]** The four sectors are not independent — they share the same 64 sites.

